From tomas at openssl.org  Thu Nov  9 08:24:54 2023
From: tomas at openssl.org (Tomas Mraz)
Date: Thu, 09 Nov 2023 09:24:54 +0100
Subject: Multi threaded aspect of loading providers
In-Reply-To: <CAKn5YzxO6QEgbp+U0+ymV=VSPo4J6wmVrnJ9OJJ8t3zqMONOQg@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CAKn5YzxO6QEgbp+U0+ymV=VSPo4J6wmVrnJ9OJJ8t3zqMONOQg@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <95cf9efdb975b4bf649d0613dd6558f94d8f2ec9.camel@openssl.org>

The providers are loaded per library context. If NULL is used as the
libctx parameter of the OSSL_PROVIDER_load() function the default
library context is used. There is one implicit global default library
context per process. However please note that you can temporarily
override per thread what the NULL parameter means by using the
OSSL_LIB_CTX_set0_default() function.

Tomas Mraz, OpenSSL

